Geno for Super Smash Bros. Melee: licences
==========================================

This repository holds two kinds of work, under two licences.

1. Code and tools: the MIT License (below)
------------------------------------------
Every program, script and build file: everything under tools/, the source code under projects/ (.py, .sh, .cs, .c, .h,
.js, .lua and the like), the director, datkit, and our own additions to the decompilation in decomp/geno.patch.

2. Documentation, art, design and audio: CC BY-NC 4.0 (LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The documents (README.md, MAKING-OF.md, HOW-TO-PLAY.md, every other .md file, including DESIGN.md, ART.md and the
research), the design itself (the moveset, its frame data and the character and stage designs as these documents and
the code describe them), our own art data (for example the ♡ and ♪ glyphs in decomp/geno.patch), and the audio in
audio/: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International.
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

Attribution: "Geno for Super Smash Bros. Melee, directed by Michael Bishop, built with Claude Code"
(https://github.com/bishpls/ssbm-geno).

What these licences don't cover
-------------------------------
This is a non-commercial fan project. Geno, Super Mario RPG and their music belong to Nintendo and Square Enix; Super
Smash Bros. Melee belongs to Nintendo and HAL Laboratory. We license only our own work:
- The audio in audio/ is our own arrangement and recording of melodies from Super Mario RPG (music by Yoko Shimomura).
  CC BY-NC 4.0 covers our arrangement and our recording, not the compositions.
- Files the build tools produce from your own Melee disc or Super Mario RPG cartridge (fighter, stage, menu and sound
  files, the game build) contain or derive from that game data. They aren't ours to license and must not be shared.
- The player patch attached to a release (an xdelta) carries a compiled build and game-derived data. It's offered for
  use with your own copy of the game only, and isn't covered by either licence.

Third-party software
--------------------
None of these is included in this repository except the two fonts.
- doldecomp/melee (https://github.com/doldecomp/melee), the Melee decompilation the patch applies to. It has no licence
  file at the base commit (64e41ca). decomp/geno.patch carries the unchanged lines around each change (diff context)
  and the lines it edits; get the decompilation itself from upstream.
- HSDLib / HSDRaw (https://github.com/Ploaj/HSDLib), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2021 Ploaj. datkit builds on it; clone it
  into vendor/HSDLib (HOW-TO-PLAY.md).
- Archivo (The Archivo Project Authors, Omnibus-Type), SIL Open Font License 1.1: engine/fonts/Archivo.ttf, licence in
  engine/fonts/OFL-archivo.txt (the review boards).
- Big Shoulders Display (The Big Shoulders Project Authors), SIL Open Font License 1.1:
  engine/fonts/BigShouldersDisplay.ttf, licence in engine/fonts/OFL-bigshouldersdisplay.txt (the Forest Maze's
  stage-select name).
- The audio in audio/ was played by third-party instruments, credited in audio/README.md. The Forest Maze track's drums
  require this credit: "Aasimonster2 drumkit by the DrumGizmo team, CC-BY 4.0".
- Used, not distributed: decomp-toolkit (dtk), wibo, the Metrowerks CodeWarrior compilers (doldecomp's configure.py
  downloads them), Dolphin, Blender, .NET, Mesen2, blargg's snes_spc (fetched and patched by the sound capture),
  vgmstream, Praat (parselmouth), xdelta3 and the Python packages in requirements.txt. The music renderer's instruments
  are listed with their licences in projects/geno/music/README.md.

